# The example extension that owns .csv files (examples/extensions/csv-table), installed in the
# empty home by tests/drive.rs. Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv shows in the tree, and Enter hands it to
# the extension, which shows it as a table. An edited cell is saved to the file; a change made by
# another program shows up in the table, and the next edit saves on top of it. A link to the file
# and the quick switcher open it too, and the extension's command makes a new table. tests/drive.rs
# then reads both files.
size 140x24
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys /
type eruptions
wait-for ▤ Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
keys enter j
wait-for CSV table · ⏎ to open it in csv-table
keys enter
wait-for [[Mount St. Helens]]  1980
expect Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
expect 4 rows
keys j l e
wait-for Year: 1883▏
keys ctrl+u
type 1884
keys enter
wait-for saved Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
expect [[Krakatoa]]          1884
write Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv Volcano,Year,VEI,Notes\n[[Vesuvius]],79,5,\n[[Krakatoa]],1884,6,- [ ] Read the Royal Society report on [[Krakatoa]] 📅 2026-11-20\n[[Mount St. Helens]],1980,5,\n[[Eyjafjallajökull]],2010,4,\n[[Tambora]],1816,7,\n
wait-for Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv changed: showing it as it is now
expect 5 rows
keys j j j e
wait-for Year: 1816▏
keys ctrl+u
type 1815
keys enter
wait-for saved Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
expect [[Tambora]]           1815
screen
keys esc esc p
type start here
wait-for Start Here
keys enter
wait-for Guide/Start Here  reading
keys tab tab tab tab tab enter
wait-for Tambora
wait-for Ctrl-o ⟵ Start Here
keys ctrl+o
wait-for Guide/Start Here  reading
keys esc p
type erupt
wait-for Eruptions.csv
expect Volcanoes  CSV table
keys enter
wait-for Tambora
keys esc :
type new csv
wait-for new CSV table
keys enter
wait-for made Untitled.csv
expect Untitled.csv
screen
keys esc q
exits 0
